WEBVTT

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.260
Say, have you heard?

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.100
Yes. I suppose the rumors were true.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.140
A "G" really will doom the royal family.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.230
George can no longer
make rational decisions.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.770
It was simple to lay the blame on him.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:33.070
I can hardly believe that
George really was cursing me.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.910
Still, I won't charge him yet.
I'll keep him under surveillance.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.410
He may come to his senses given time.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.750
But what example will it set
if he goes unpunished for--

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:48.920
Richard, I could not be more
grateful for your efforts.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.760
It's a little early,
but this banquet is over!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.920
Your Majesty!

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.010
Yes, your health comes first.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.140
We should have killed him.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.760
That's always the way.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.310
Hope makes people mad.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.890
I wish for a family celebration today.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.900
Richard!

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.610
We're going out on the town tonight!
Join us!

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.700
York of the white rose.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.280
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:27.790
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:32.420
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.770
Your Majesty!
Please make yourself at home!

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:15.150
I've brought my brothers along!

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:20.490
I thought Your Majesty had forgotten us
in your obsession with that woman.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:23.530
She's a rose, but you're lilies.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.660
All flowers are beautiful.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.700
I'm so disgusted I'm actually impressed.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.790
This isn't the first time.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.580
I'll simply wait it out as I always do.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.960
Tell the king I enjoyed myself.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.130
I'll while the time away as I see fit.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.510
Please. I'll work for my pay.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:48.600
I'll merely do as I'm bid,
as long as it's for York.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.350
How rude!

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:53.020
What's this? A whore putting on airs?

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.480
Drink up!

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.940
Wh-Who the devil are you?!

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.940
The Duke of Gloucester,

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.490
Richard Plantagenet.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.910
B-Beg pardon, Your Grace!

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:09.870
Thank you, Richard!

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.540
Are you drunk, Beth?

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.290
I know! Let's party together!

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:21.510
No. This place isn't proper for you to--

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.470
Then we'll go out on the town!

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:27.140
I've always wanted to see it!

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:29.560
Look at this! Doesn't it suit me?

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:36.020
A princess out at night in men's garb?
What's the world coming to?

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:38.690
It's better than letting
her run off alone.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.400
Please bless me!

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.530
May the Lord save me,
whom my parents abandoned!

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:48.280
Sin begot sickness,
and a demon took hold of my flesh!

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.240
What difference is there
between him and me?

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:55.290
Without the protective cloak of rank and
name, this body would make me like him.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.170
I've seen you before.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:01.710
We've met somewhere,
haven't we, my good sir?

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:02.630
Get back.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:04.340
Too good for me, are you?!

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:08.510
You look like some drifter,
just like we are!

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.470
Just like him?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.270
Yes! I won!

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:20.900
Remember, you all swore to obey
the "king's" orders if you lost!

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:23.230
I'm as good as my word.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.900
Command me, Your Majesty.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.070
Ahem!

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:29.570
Very well. Your sovereign orders you...

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:34.120
...to each tell me who
your first love was!

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.500
No one.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.630
What?! No way! What about your wife?!

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.710
Never.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:45.550
Unbelievable. I was hoping
for some lovely stories.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:48.680
You'll both tell me something
romantic, won't you?

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:51.810
It was my wife.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.850
I knew it!

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:59.560
You married your first love!
You and Anne really are a perfect couple!

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.440
And what about you, Catesby?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.070
I'm curious as well.

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:07.860
Did a stick in the mud like you
ever care for women?

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.610
Ridiculous. Of course not.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:10.620
Yes.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:17.580
I have loved only one person in my life.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.500
What is she like? Are you still together?

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.630
I had no idea you cared
for anyone in that way.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:29.630
Is this person kind?

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:31.470
They are.

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:32.930
I see.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:35.520
--Your Grace--
--I'm king this time.

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:39.310
I've decided on my order.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:44.980
Richard, kiss whichever
of us you most trust.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.360
Your Grace!

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.240
You can't do that!

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:52.160
It's a royal command.
Aren't you the most loyal of all?

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:00.790
Hope makes people mad.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:08.170
It's just as you said, Buckingham.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.300
Merely a jest, Richard.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:13.970
Is it over?

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:17.430
Yes. That's enough of nightlife.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:29.610
A long time ago, he carried me
a long way on his back.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.370
People don't change.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:39.620
If you feel as though someone has,
you just didn't know them well enough.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.590
Richard, become ruthless.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:48.920
You still have hope for people.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:54.010
If you give that up, you'll be able
to have hope for yourself.

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:55.800
Like you do?

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:56.970
Yes.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.890
I am like no one else.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:07.150
I am myself alone.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:12.990
If this body gives me any cause
for hope, it is only my blood.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:17.280
The blood of York will conceal
the sin of this body.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:21.580
Not even God can overcome its authority.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:24.540
Buckingham.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:29.800
Kill George.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.590
As you wish.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:41.140
I know an assassin named James Tyrrell.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:45.980
He will perform any dirty job
to perfect so long as he is paid.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:49.020
I'll convey your orders to his go-between.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:51.360
Simply killing him is not enough.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:55.740
With George gone,
the queen's power will grow.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.780
Then we need only convince the king

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:02.370
that the Woodvilles drove
George to his death.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:03.870
Tell me your plan.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:09.920
Richard, you're going to
see George, aren't you?

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.630
Hello, Mother.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:16.470
I knew that this day
would come eventually.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:17.930
What do you mean?

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:20.850
Lady Cecily!

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.220
Richard!

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.770
You may fool the rest of them,
but never me!

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:27.770
You're a demon that destroys everything!

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.610
O Lord!

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.730
Please keep my dear sons safe!

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:41.240
M-Mother...?

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:42.540
George.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:45.960
Richard?!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:50.090
G-Give me wine!
This is more than I can bear!

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:53.300
A sentence of death
will be pronounced today.

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:56.010
Impossible! I haven't been
summoned to court!

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.180
Those demons that thrive around
the king arranged it all.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:02.720
So, the Woodvilles are to blame!

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:06.600
George, I can't leave you like this.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.190
Richard.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:11.520
You're the only ally I have.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:15.940
Yes. I'll save you,
even if I must take your place.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:27.870
That man's crimes against
His Royal Majesty are unpardonable.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:31.420
They are an act of treason
and an affront to God!

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:32.750
Thus, capital punishment is--

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:33.750
Wait!

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:37.130
Do you mean to murder me
without so much as a trial?!

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.510
Who called for my execution?!

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:40.890
You there! Seize him!

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:43.560
Quiet, you shameless Woodville!

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:46.730
You've risen in rank,
but your soul's as lowly as ever!

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:49.480
Go back to hell, you clan of demons!

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:51.310
I will not hear this.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:52.940
Listen, everyone!

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:57.690
Demons are manipulating the king
into selling England to the devil!

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:00.030
I am their human sacrifice!

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.910
Edward is a murderer!

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.490
--Someone, seize him this instant!
--This faithless king must pay!

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.200
Don't touch me!

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.790
If you kill me, you'll go to hell!

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:13.710
God would thank his killer.

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:16.170
It's high time you told your brother

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:18.630
that he's not the man on trial here.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:25.470
Die for the royal family anointed by God,

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:26.600
my brother.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.270
This is open rebellion!

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:37.360
He called us a clan of demons
in front of everyone!

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:39.690
He must certainly be stripped of power.

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:42.660
Too lenient!
This isn't his first betrayal!

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:47.790
Your Majesty, the queen has suffered
the greatest slight to her honor.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:50.620
My honor is of little concern.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:57.130
But a slight to the king's honor must not
go unpunished no matter its source.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:58.550
If he lets it stand...

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.550
We'll have a real rebellion next!

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:04.300
Treason will beget further treason.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.350
Your Majesty!

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.980
Send wine to his cell.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:12.850
Before his execution.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:25.660
I doubt Mother will ever forgive me.

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:29.330
George was always her favorite.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:36.460
When we were little, she would tell him
stories about the witch of the forest.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:42.090
They scared him so much that
he'd come to hide in my bed.

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:46.760
He'd say that children who got lost
in the woods became witches.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:49.350
He thought I became a witch?

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:52.640
He's a pure soul; he'll believe anything.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:57.270
Divine miracles and
demonic whisperings alike.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:00.610
Who's there?

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.900
You're no guard.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:06.240
My last supper?

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:10.870
Royal dignity didn't amount
to much in the end.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:15.250
I merely exchanged peaceful
rest for suspicion and sorrow.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:19.420
I never dreamed of this back then.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:25.720
I assumed that family ties
would last forever.

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:30.720
But I have one hope left.
One last ray of light.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:35.940
Only my little brother.
He promised to save me.

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:42.650
George was a bungling man,
but a lovable brother.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:48.160
He did betray me once,
but he returned to me in the end.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.080
He swore his fealty to me.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:58.210
I don't wish to feud with him anymore,
but I can't avoid fraternal conflict.

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:01.090
Not so long as I am king.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.420
He sent you to rescue me?

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:09.050
How compassionate he is.

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:11.970
Please take your rest, Brother.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.260
No.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:14.770
It won't do.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.520
I'll rescind the order.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:18.690
I'll cancel George's execution!

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:22.400
Yes. Let us spare him.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:23.900
Richard.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:26.150
Are you Richard's man?

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:28.490
Here to rescue--

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.870
Where do I know you from?

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:45.670
No.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.800
Please... Save me.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:50.340
Good night.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:51.550
Brother.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:06.570
Jewels, gold...

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:08.150
What good are they now?

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:16.290
Oh. This must be hell.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:23.250
George.

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:47.690
George is dead?
But I countermanded his execution.

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.740
He likely took his own life in his grief.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.030
Why?!

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:54.320
Why did no one plead for his life?!

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:58.370
Why did no one warn me not
to take my brother's life?!

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:01.830
Far from it, you incited me
to order his death!

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:03.380
All of you did!

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:06.380
--What? But...
--Leave us! This instant!

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:09.510
--Your Majesty!
--Your Majesty!

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:10.670
Your Majesty!

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:12.090
Stay strong!

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:14.800
This is absurd!

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:17.310
He plans to blame this all on us?!

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:20.430
He wanted George gone more than anyone!

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:23.770
He may be secretly relieved,
but he can't show it.

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:26.150
How dare you besmirch His Majesty!

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:29.400
It seems His Majesty's
survival is in doubt.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:34.660
Now George is dead, what will
happen if the king dies, too?

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.070
Perish the thought!

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:38.200
There's nothing to worry about.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:42.250
He has a fine, legitimate
prince to succeed him.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:48.920
The prince is still a child.
He'll need someone to govern for him.

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:51.420
And I suppose you think
that should be you?!

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:53.430
With George gone,

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:58.390
is not the king's brother, the Duke
of Gloucester, the natural choice?

00:16:58.390 --> 00:16:59.810
W-Well...

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:04.020
Nevertheless, when you consider
how we Woodvilles have labored for--

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:08.570
Richard and the rest of us have been
shedding blood for His Majesty!

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:12.400
We've been fighting for him since
the Woodvilles were Lancastrian!

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:14.650
Isn't that right, Your Majesty?

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:16.280
Lord Hastings!

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:21.200
Yes, it is.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:24.710
And my husband died
in battle at St. Albans.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:30.300
His corpse was disgracefully
plundered and dumped in an alley,

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:33.260
leaving only this single memento.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:42.640
I am no longer the widowed Lady Grey.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:48.860
I am the wife of Edward Plantagenet
and the Queen of England!

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.230
Your Majesty.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:54.070
Please, all of you, be silent.

00:17:55.360 --> 00:18:00.120
To squabble on a day like this is
an insult to my brother's passing.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:06.580
Despising each other as foes is
a suffering more bitter than death.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:09.750
I can endure no more such torment.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:15.720
W-Well said. I may have
been a touch indecorous.

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:18.260
Forgive me, Richard.

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:28.100
I'm impressed. You silenced mighty
nobles with a single tear.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:31.020
Not even a witch could do that.

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:35.900
This makes one less person
between you and the throne.

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:38.490
Who will it be next? The princes?

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:40.030
The king?

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:45.120
I will merely eliminate anyone
who threatens the royal family.

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.580
Even someone you love?

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.790
Yes.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:54.710
I even killed the person
I love most in this world.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.800
I'll return to my duchy for now.

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:04.810
What a ruckus.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:08.690
Your Grace, allow me to deliver a warning

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:12.480
about your precious sovereign.

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:16.360
A man in the city is spreading
rumors about his body's secret.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:19.780
What secret?

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:22.700
Oh, my. Don't tell me you didn't know.

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:24.410
Explain yourself.

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:26.750
Why not investigate for yourself?

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:30.580
A secret?

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:33.460
He swore that he had none from me!

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.200
There's no reason to mourn.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:05.580
It will all serve to sustain
our precious York.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:11.750
Who's there? No one is to enter
my chambers without--

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.540
I'm sorry.

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.340
What's wrong?

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:18.760
I had a dream that you
passed away, Father.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:23.430
There was a war, and you... you...

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:35.940
I've emerged victorious from many battles.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.860
I won't die so easily.

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:40.740
Truly?

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:44.450
I need my son to have more courage.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:47.950
You're the Earl of Salisbury now.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.330
Do you feel better?

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:54.120
I want you to hug me.

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:58.250
I-I'm sorry! I'll get stronger!

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:00.630
Come here.

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:11.180
Please! Listen to what I have to say!

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:14.020
A demon in the palace? Don't talk rubbish.

00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:15.900
Listen! This is important!

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:18.310
I haven't got time for your fantasies!

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:19.690
It's true!

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:22.360
He's the demon child from back then!

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:24.320
Listen to me!

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:29.870
Your Grace. What brings you here?

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:32.040
What brings you?

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.500
Of course.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:36.250
You've been a loyal servant to our king.

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:38.210
Tell me.

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:41.760
What secret does Richard's body hide?

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:43.420
So, you do know.

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:45.800
Why didn't Richard tell me?

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:47.840
Speak! What are you hiding?!

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:56.230
I'll make anyone who harms him pay,
whomever they may be!

00:21:57.310 --> 00:21:58.440
Your Grace!

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:00.020
His Royal Majesty has...!
